  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equipping Law Enforcement Officers with Skills to Handle Technology-Facilitated Violence Against Children</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The justice system in Kenya is currently unable to effectively address cases of Technology Facilitated Violence against Children (TFVAC).  The alarming rise in cases of online child sexual exploitation and abuse (OCSEA), as reported by the Anti-Human Trafficking and Child Protection Unit (AHTCPU) of the Directorate of Criminal Investigations (DCI), underscores the urgent need for enhanced measures to safeguard children in this urban center. Kisumu and Nakuru cities have high internet accessibility rates and significant impact of TFVAC on urban children. The project aims to target areas where children are most vulnerable to online violence and abuse. Implementing comprehensive training programs, institutional integration efforts and standardized procedures in the two counties will enhance the limited expertise capacity and enable law enforcement agencies to effectively respond to TFVAC cases and protect children from harm in this urban environment.</narrative>
  </description>
